    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "As spring weather brought more favorable conditions for travel, the number of apprehensions along the U.S. border surged from February to March, revealing a renewed push by boundary-crossers to navigate the frontier zone. While this uptick is notable, analysts point out that immigration statistics show year-to-date crossings remain near multi-decade lows, a result of recent enforcement policies that have reshaped the migration landscape. The pattern highlights how policy shifts continue to define this geopolitical region.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The border security agency is observing a seasonal spike, with crossing attempts surging along the frontier in the wake of milder spring weather. Despite this activity, the legislative stalemate in Washington persists, leaving funding for enforcement agencies in limbo. This ongoing political deadlock prevents policy innovators from charting new routes to address the complex flow of migrants, underscoring a tension between on-the-ground realities and institutional gridlock.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.75
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Frontier watchers note a clear numerical change: apprehensions climbed significantly in March as spring weather drew more people to the southwest border. This movement occurs against a backdrop of stringent asylum shutdowns that have kept overall immigration statistics at historic lows. The situation presents a stark image of a walled jurisdiction confronting human flow, while the broader political impasse over funding shows no signs of resolution.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
